/target

# git worktrees for isolated feature work
.worktrees/
.claude/

# Lane status: a claim about right now, deliberately volatile, and the contract
# (empyrean contract/LANE_STATUS.md rule 5) makes local disk authoritative and
# tracking the lane's own call. Untracked-and-not-ignored was the third state:
# it left `sigil --version` reporting `tree: dirty` permanently, for a file no
# build reads, so consumers pinning this assembler read a warning that could
# never turn off. Durable history belongs in the committed docs/lane-log.jsonl.
docs/lane-status.json

# The golden freeze's staging area (golden/atomic_freeze.sh). A leftover one is
# announced by the next `capture_goldens.sh --write`, which refuses over it; it is
# ignored here so a killed capture cannot leave untracked `.bin` files in a shared
# checkout for a later `git add` to sweep up.
crates/sigil-harness/golden/.staging/

# The freeze's completion journal (crates/sigil-harness/src/freeze_journal.rs). It is a
# claim about a run in flight — present only while `refreeze --freeze` is running or
# after one was killed — so it is never durable history, and ignoring it keeps a killed
# run from leaving an untracked file for a later `git add` to sweep into a commit. Its
# ABSENCE is what says a freeze completed; `refreeze --check` refuses while it is here.
crates/sigil-harness/golden/.freeze-journal

# dedicated landing-verification target dir — never share target/ between worktrees
/.target-land/

# scripts/provision-aeon-ref.sh's build directory when the caller names none
# (scripts/lib/sigil_tool.sh, sigil_tool_ref_target step 3). Per-worktree by
# construction: the predecessor default was one path outside the checkout, shared by
# every worktree of this repo, which is the artifact-substitution fault that function
# now refuses.
/.target-ref/

# scripts/tree_state_capture_gate.sh's own target dir. That gate asserts the tree is
# clean before it mutates anything, so a build artifact of its own showing up as an
# untracked file would refuse the very run it is part of. Ignored, not relocated to
# target/: that one is a shared artifact other lanes pin by hash.
/.target-tree-state-gate/
/.target-tree-state-gate.buildlog
